(20)Simple End-to-End CI/CD Pipeline

🔹 Step 1: Create Maven Web Project
Open Command Prompt
Run:
mvn archetype:generate
Choose:
3 → org.apache.maven.archetypes:maven-archetype-webapp
Enter:
GroupId: com.demo
ArtifactId: webapp
Version: 1.0-SNAPSHOT
Package: com.demo
🔹 Step 2: Add Java Folder (IMPORTANT)

By default Maven webapp does NOT create java folder

So create manually:

webapp/src/main/java/com/demo/
🔹 Step 3: Add Servlet Code

Create file:

HelloServlet.java

Paste:

package com.demo;
import java.io.*;
import javax.servlet.*;
import javax.servlet.http.*;

public class HelloServlet extends HttpServlet {
    public void doGet(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse res) throws IOException {
        res.getWriter().println("CI/CD OK");
    }
}
🔹 Step 4: Update index.jsp

Path:

src/main/webapp/index.jsp

Code:

<h1>CI/CD Demo</h1>
<a href="hello">Run</a>
🔹 Step 5: Update web.xml

Path:

src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/web.xml

Add:

<servlet>
<servlet-name>hello</servlet-name>
<servlet-class>com.demo.HelloServlet</servlet-class>
</servlet>

<servlet-mapping>
<servlet-name>hello</servlet-name>
<url-pattern>/hello</url-pattern>
</servlet-mapping>
🔹 Step 6: Update pom.xml

Add dependency:

<dependency>
<groupId>javax.servlet</groupId>
<artifactId>javax.servlet-api</artifactId>
<version>4.0.1</version>
<scope>provided</scope>
</dependency>

Also ensure:

<packaging>war</packaging>
🔹 Step 7: Build Project
mvn clean package

✔ WAR file will be created inside:

target/webapp.war
🔹 Step 8: Create Dockerfile

In root folder:

Dockerfile
FROM tomcat:9
COPY target/webapp.war /usr/local/tomcat/webapps/
